nced requires the upsells. A 70-bed property priced at $13 a night without =
an F&amp;B program will operate at a loss for its first several years becau=
se the fixed costs of Costa Rican labor, utilities, and real estate outpace=
 the budget nightly rate. The bar and the chef are what actually pay the mo=
