True Labor &amp; Utility Cost Matrix
Costa Rican labor law heavily protects employees. The base salary is only t=
he starting point; employers must pay roughly 27% in CCSS (Caja) social and=
 parafiscal charges, plus accrue 8% monthly to fund the mandatory "Aguinald=
o" (a 13th-month bonus paid every December). Utilities, particularly electr=
icity, rank among the highest in Latin America.</p>
