<h2 dir=3D"auto" class=3D"font-semibold text-2xl mt-[1.5em] max-md:font-dis=
play max-md:text-heading-2 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md:tracking-[0.17px] m=
ax-md:mb-3 max-md:mt-3 md:streamdown-last-block:mb-0">What was wrong and wh=
at changed</h2>
<p dir=3D"auto" class=3D"break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md=
:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0 streamdown-first-block:mt-0" style=3D"white-space: p=
re-wrap;">Gemini=E2=80=99s story was directionally right on one point: at b=
ackpacker ADRs, <strong class=3D"font-semibold">beds are a thin cover for C=
osta Rican fixed cost</strong>. Almost every supporting number was loose.</=
p>
<p dir=3D"auto" class=3D"break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md=
:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0 streamdown-first-block:mt-0" style=3D"white-space: p=
re-wrap;"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">The reference property is not =E2=
=80=9C70 identical $13 beds.=E2=80=9D</strong> Costa Rica Backpackers (Av. =
6, C. 21=E2=80=9323) is a mixed house: 4/6/8-bed dorms plus privates, resta=
urant, bar, pool, garden, fans not AC, tour desk, breakfast ~$6, coworking =
$5/day. HostelsClub lists <strong class=3D"font-semibold">15 private rooms =
and 19 dorm rooms</strong>. Scrapers that say =E2=80=9C95 bedrooms=E2=80=9D=
 are garbage. The model defaults to a <strong class=3D"font-semibold">48-be=
d / 12-private replica</strong>, which is the honest unit of analysis.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto" class=3D"break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md=
:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0 streamdown-first-block:mt-0" style=3D"white-space: p=
re-wrap;"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Labor was understated.</strong> 2=
026 employer cargas are <strong class=3D"font-semibold">26.83%</strong>, no=
t a vibes-based 26.5%. That still excludes the 13th month (<strong class=3D=
"font-semibold">aguinaldo 8.33%</strong>) and vacation accrual. Planning lo=
ad is <strong class=3D"font-semibold">base =C3=97 1.38=E2=80=931.45</strong=
>. Unskilled minimum is =E2=82=A1373,092/month =E2=89=88 <strong class=3D"f=
ont-semibold">$829 at =E2=82=A1450</strong>, not Gemini=E2=80=99s $720 clea=
ner.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto" class=3D"break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md=
:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0 streamdown-first-block:mt-0" style=3D"white-space: p=
re-wrap;"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Tax was a brochure.</strong> Ordi=
nary CIT is <strong class=3D"font-semibold">30%</strong> once you leave the=
 SME gross-income window =E2=80=94 a 60-bed hostel with a bar will. Dividen=
d WHT to a non-resident owner is <strong class=3D"font-semibold">15%</stron=
g>. IVA <strong class=3D"font-semibold">13%</strong> applies to short-stay =
lodging, F&amp;B, and laundry and is <strong class=3D"font-semibold">not re=
venue</strong>. There is <strong class=3D"font-semibold">no US=E2=80=93CR i=
ncome tax treaty</strong>. FEIE ($132,900 in 2026) covers <em>earned</em> s=
ervices abroad; <strong class=3D"font-semibold">dividends from an S.R.L. ar=
e not FEIE</strong>, and if capital is material the IRS caps the earned sli=
ce at <strong class=3D"font-semibold">30% of net</strong>. A faith-based as=
ociaci=C3=B3n does not zero-out a commercial bunkhouse.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto" class=3D"break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md=
:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0 streamdown-first-block:mt-0" style=3D"white-space: p=
re-wrap;"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Occupancy is not a 65% =C2=B115 b=
ell curve.</strong> CCH=E2=80=99s YE25/26 hotel survey is a <em>peak</em> p=
rint (national 77%, Guanacaste 88%, city ~60=E2=80=9368%). Annual hostel oc=
cupancy is a dry/green problem. National short-let occupancy is much worse =
because listings roughly <strong class=3D"font-semibold">doubled</strong> s=
ince 2019. The model uses regional ceilings and a Y1=E2=80=93Y3 ramp, not a=
 fake normal distribution.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto" class=3D"break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md=
:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0 streamdown-first-block:mt-0" style=3D"white-space: p=
re-wrap;"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">OTA fees only hit rooms.</strong>=
 Charging 15% of bar and laundry was a P&amp;L error.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto" class=3D"break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md=
:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0 streamdown-first-block:mt-0" style=3D"white-space: p=
re-wrap;"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">The col=C3=B3n is a line item.</s=
trong> Mid-September 2026 prints around <strong class=3D"font-semibold">=E2=
=82=A1447</strong>, strongest since 2007 records. You collect dollars and p=
ay Caja in colones. Arrivals can rise (2.19m Jan=E2=80=93Aug 2026, +5.3%) w=
hile USD margins shrink.</p>
<h2 dir=3D"auto" class=3D"font-semibold text-2xl mt-[1.5em] max-md:font-dis=
play max-md:text-heading-2 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md:tracking-[0.17px] m=
ax-md:mb-3 max-md:mt-3 md:streamdown-last-block:mb-0">How to use the desk</=
h2>
<ol dir=3D"auto" class=3D"marker:text-secondary">
<li class=3D"break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-norma=
l [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Pick a <strong class=3D"font-semibold">r=
egion preset</strong> =E2=80=94 San Jos=C3=A9, Liberia, Tamarindo, Jac=C3=
=B3, Fortuna, Monteverde, Caribe, Osa. ADR, occupancy, utilities, rent, and=
 attach rates move together.</li>
<li class=3D"break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-norma=
l [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Pick a <strong class=3D"font-semibold">w=
rapper</strong> =E2=80=94 persona f=C3=ADsica, S.R.L., S.A., US LLC stack, =
C-Corp stack, asociaci=C3=B3n. Owner cash after CR CIT + WHT changes; US GI=
LTI/5471 is flagged in the entity tab, not pretended away.</li>
<li class=3D"break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-norma=
l [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Toggle <strong class=3D"font-semibold">a=
ncillaries off</strong>. The beds-only column is still the right stress tes=
t. Tours are modeled as <em>net commission</em>, not fake ticket volume.</l=
i>
<li class=3D"break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-norma=
l [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Read <strong class=3D"font-semibold">bre=
ak-even occupancy</strong> and the <strong class=3D"font-semibold">ADR =C3=
=97 occupancy grid</strong> before you believe Year 10.</li>
</ol>
<p dir=3D"auto" class=3D"break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md=
:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0 streamdown-first-block:mt-0" style=3D"white-space: p=
re-wrap;">Default San Jos=C3=A9 replica with F&amp;B/tours on, 58% occupanc=
y, $16 dorms, $55 privates, $4,200 rent, 8 loaded FTEs at $1,450: rooms alo=
ne are tight; the bar, laundry, and tour desk are what clear Caja. That con=
clusion survives the audit. Gemini=E2=80=99s $24k Year-1 profit on a styliz=
ed 70-bed, $13, no-IVA, underloaded-labor book does not.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto" class=3D"break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md=
:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0 streamdown-first-block:mt-0" style=3D"white-space: p=
re-wrap;">Not legal, tax, or immigration advice =E2=80=94 decree bands and =
ICT practice move. The entity tab is the part that actually differs from a =
US LLC vs an S-corp conversation: ownership is easy, <strong class=3D"font-=
semibold">working the desk on a tourist stamp is not</strong>, and inversio=
nista ($150k, often titled in your own name) is a residency path, not a lab=
or-law exemption.</p></div></div></div></div><section class=3D"inline-media=
