    <!-- =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D AU=
DIT =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D -->
    <section id=3D"tab-audit" class=3D"tabpane hidden space-y-4">
      <div class=3D"kpi rounded-xl p-5">
        <h2 class=3D"text-lg font-semibold">Fact audit of the prior model &=
amp; the Gemini memo</h2>
        <p class=3D"text-sm text-slate-400 mt-2">Directionally Gemini was r=
ight about one thing: at $13 bunks, labor + occupancy cost can eat the room=
. The supporting numbers were rounded folklore. This desk replaces them wit=
h 2026 public sources and says where the tape is thin.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"overflow-x-auto kpi rounded-xl p-4">
        <table class=3D"data w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class=3D"text-left py-2">Claim</th>
              <th class=3D"text-left">Prior take</th>
              <th class=3D"text-left">Corrected 2026 position</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class=3D"text-slate-300 align-top">
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">Reference hostel si=
ze</td>
              <td>User memory =E2=80=9C~70 people.=E2=80=9D Gemini modeled =
70 identical dorm beds at $13.</td>
              <td>Costa Rica Backpackers is a mixed-inventory house: 4/6/8-=
bed dorms plus privates, restaurant, bar, pool, garden, fans not AC, tour d=
esk, breakfast ~$6, coworking $5. HostelsClub: 15 private rooms + 19 dorm r=
ooms. Public room-count scrapers that say =E2=80=9C95 bedrooms=E2=80=9D are=
 junk. Model a mixed stack.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">Dorm ADR</td>
              <td>$13 blending up to $18 by Y10. SJ =E2=80=9Cmedian $15.=E2=
=80=9D</td>
              <td>2026 backpacker guides put major-destination dorms around=
 $14=E2=80=9332. SJ floor still exists near $10=E2=80=9315 on OTAs in soft =
weeks; Tamarindo/Jaco/Santa Teresa print $18=E2=80=9340. Selina-class produ=
ct is a different ADR family. Use regional presets, not one national median=
.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">Occupancy 65% =C2=
=B115pp as a law of nature</td>
              <td>Bell curve presented as property physics.</td>
              <td>CCH peak survey YE25/26: national hotel 77% projected, Va=
lle Central city ~60=E2=80=9368%, Guanacaste 88%. That is high season hotel=
s, not annual hostels. Short-let occupancy nationally is much worse (high-2=
0s to mid-40s) because listings doubled. A well-run SJ transit hostel can d=
o mid-50s to mid-60s annual; a beach poshtel can beat that in dry months an=
d fall into the 30s in October. Seasonality is the model, not a single =CF=
=83.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">Employer Caja =E2=
=80=9C~26.5%=E2=80=9D</td>
              <td>Used as the full labor burden.</td>
              <td>2026 employer package 26.83% (IVM +0.16pp). Add aguinaldo=
 8.33% and vacation and you plan 38=E2=80=9345% on base. Gemini=E2=80=99s $=
720 cleaner is below the 2026 unskilled minimum (=E2=82=A1373,092 =E2=89=88=
 $829 at 450).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">Corporate tax =E2=
=80=9C5=E2=80=9330%=E2=80=9D</td>
              <td>Quoted as if every hostel picks a rate from a menu.</td>
              <td>30% is the ordinary CIT. 5/10/15/20% is an SME scale gate=
d by annual gross. Dividend WHT to a non-resident owner is 15% (5% listed-s=
hare exception). Law 9428 annual company tax is extra.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">US FEIE on =E2=80=
=9Cthe hostel=E2=80=9D</td>
              <td>Implied the profit lands in the exclusion.</td>
              <td>FEIE 2026 cap $132,900 is for foreign <em>earned</em> inc=
ome. Dividends from an S.R.L. are not earned. If capital is material, IRS c=
aps the earned slice at 30% of net. No US=E2=80=93CR income tax treaty. FTC=
 is the tool for CIT/WHT. FBAR / 8938 / 5471 still exist.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">Nonprofit =3D 0%</t=
d>
              <td>Table cell said 0% if =E2=80=9Cpublic utility.=E2=80=9D</=
td>
              <td>Utilidad p=C3=BAblica is a political/administrative grant=
, not a checkbox. IVA still hits commercial guest charges. Hacienda audits =
mixed-purpose associations. Do not underwrite a yield hostel as a church.</=
td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">IVA</td>
              <td>Missing from both the HTML app and the Gemini P&amp;L.</t=
d>
              <td>13% on short-stay lodging, F&amp;B, most extras. Collect =
and remit. Platforms are being deputized as withhold agents.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">OTA 15% of total re=
venue</td>
              <td>Applied to F&amp;B too.</td>
              <td>Commission is on the booked room (and sometimes packages)=
. Bar tabs and laundry at the desk are not Hostelworld=E2=80=99s. Use an OT=
A mix on room revenue only.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">Insurance $200=E2=
=80=93900 / month as =E2=80=9Cutils=E2=80=9D</td>
              <td>Lumped into a wide band with water.</td>
              <td>INS hogar-style quotes on a $600k house can be ~$1.6k/yea=
r. Commercial RC + fire on a hostel is higher than a house but Gemini=E2=80=
=99s high monthly print looks like replacement-cost coastal luxury, not a S=
J fan house.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">$72k rent as destin=
y</td>
              <td>Hard-coded in both scenarios.</td>
              <td>Hotel listings median asking ~$1.35m nationally; commerci=
al median asking ~$799k =E2=80=94 means are higher. SJ apartments ~$2,000=
=E2=80=933,000/m=C2=B2. Tamarindo median asking on tracked inventory is lux=
ury-tilted (~$690k). Foreigners rarely get cheap long amortizing CRC mortga=
ges. Underwrite lease vs purchase as two models.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">FX</td>
              <td>Silent.</td>
              <td>September 2026 col=C3=B3n around =E2=82=A1447, strongest =
since 2007 records. You collect dollars and pay wages in colones =E2=80=94 =
until you don=E2=80=99t. A strong col=C3=B3n compresses USD margins even wh=
en arrivals are up (ICT: 2.19m arrivals Jan=E2=80=93Aug 2026, +5.3% vs 2025=
, with a soft August US print).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class=3D"py-3 text-white font-medium">Law 6990 as a free =
lunch</td>
              <td>Mentioned as property-tax holidays and duty-free FF&amp;E=
.</td>
              <td>Real statute. Real ICT process. Not automatic for a 48-be=
d hostel that looks like a converted house. Model zero incentive until a la=
wyer and an architect have a filing plan.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class=3D"text-xs text-slate-500 pb-8">This page is an analytical w=
orkbook, not legal, tax, immigration, or investment advice. Decree numbers,=
 CRC bands, and ICT practice move. Pull Hacienda, MTSS, CCSS, ARESEP, and c=
ounsel before you wire a deposit.</p>
    </section>
  </main>




